      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "word = input()\nuses = {}\nresult = \"\"\nfor letter in word:\n    count = uses.get(letter, 0)\n    result += chr(97 + (ord(letter) - 97 + count) % 26)\n    uses[letter] = count + 1\nprint(result)\n",
      "statement": "Each lowercase letter has its own stamp.\n\nRead [[word]] from left to right. The first time a letter's stamp is used, it prints that letter. Each time the same stamp is used again, it prints the next letter in the alphabet compared with its previous use.\n\nAfter {{z}}, it wraps back to {{a}}.\n\nPrint the resulting [[stamped_word]].",
